# ChefBot settings. install.sh copies this to ~/.config/chefbot/chefbot.env the first time it runs.
# Edit that copy, then: systemctl --user restart chefbot
# Names use the app's own setting names, with __ between sections. Every setting, and the ones changed in the web
# page instead: docs/admin/settings.md (https://jamiethenextkevinbaconhamm.github.io/chef-bot/admin/settings/).
# ChefBot runs its own database inside the container, with a password it makes itself, so there is nothing to set
# for it here. Everything it keeps is in the chefbot-data volume (Data__Root=/data).

# HTTPS: SelfSigned makes ChefBot create its own certificate. Off serves HTTP only, for example behind a
# reverse proxy that handles HTTPS.
Https__Mode=SelfSigned
# The names and addresses people use to reach ChefBot, for the first certificate.
#Https__Hostnames=chefbot.local,192.168.1.20
# The HTTPS port people type. Change it if you change the HTTPS port in chefbot.container.
Https__PublicPort=8443
# Behind a reverse proxy that handles HTTPS: set Https__Mode=Off above and list the proxy here.
#Https__TrustedProxies=10.0.0.5

# The number of people, the weekly plan, leftovers, calendar meal times, the webhook and the advanced planning
# settings are changed in the app, under Settings.

# Lost the admin password? Set this to the username, restart, and read the reset link with
# journalctl --user -u chefbot. Remove it afterwards.
#Accounts__RecoverUsername=
